(Title) Tj
T*
(Antenatal Physical Activity as a Preventive Strategy Against Postpartum Mood Disorder: A) Tj
T*
(Randomized Controlled Trial Protocol) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Postpartum depression affects a substantial proportion of women and impairs maternal-) Tj
T*
(infant bonding and family functioning. Physical activity is known to influence mood) Tj
T*
(regulation and stress resilience. This protocol describes a single-center randomized trial) Tj
T*
(designed to test whether a structured aerobic exercise regimen initiated during early) Tj
T*
(pregnancy and maintained through mid-gestation reduces the incidence of postpartum) Tj
T*
(depression in women with uncomplicated pregnancies. Approximately 400 pregnant women will) Tj
T*
(be enrolled at the first prenatal visit and randomly assigned to either participate in a) Tj
T*
(supervised aerobic exercise program \(three 60-minute sessions per week\) or continue with) Tj
T*
(standard prenatal care. The primary outcome is postpartum depressive symptom severity at) Tj
T*
(three months postpartum, measured by validated screening instruments. Secondary outcomes) Tj
T*
(include clinical diagnosis rates, neonatal outcomes, and maternal physical and metabolic) Tj
T*
(parameters. We hypothesize that maintained prenatal aerobic activity reduces postpartum) Tj
T*
(depression through multiple pathways including improved mood regulation and stress coping.) Tj
